<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vata pagan uprising</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1046</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vata pagan uprising was a revolt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> in 1046, led by a nobleman named Vata, against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> and the rule of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-orseolo">Peter Orseolo</a>. The rebels killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerard-of-csanad">Gerard of Csanád</a> and other clergy and overthrew Peter, but Andrew I, whom they helped to the throne, restored the church. A second pagan rising led by Vata's son János followed in 1061.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vata-pagan-uprising.jpg" alt="Vata pagan uprising" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User Váradi Zsolt on hu.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Szent_gell%C3%A9rt_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
